## Commercial Purposes

Commercial purposes include, without limitation:

1.  any use by a commercial entity, even if for a noncommercial purpose;

2.  any use by an individual or entity for a purpose that provides a
    financial return or commercial benefit, such as charging fees for
    products or services, generating revenue, advertising, or operating
    a business; and

3.  any use as part of an effort to produce products or provide
    services that compete with products or services provided by the
    licensor.

For the avoidance of doubt, noncommercial purposes include use by:

1.  individuals for personal, educational, research, or hobby purposes,
    without any purpose that provides a financial return or commercial
    benefit; and

2.  tax-exempt charitable entities, for purposes that do not provide
    a financial return or commercial benefit.

